type like teleportation will just be irrelevant for the question we had
discussed here. We just spoke (for comparison) of the scrolls with highest
random generation probability, which were the scroll of identify, the scroll
of light, and the scroll an enchant weapon. Probably the key to understand
here is that those scrolls are *not* from the class of monster equipment;
if found on the monster's remains they are always from random death-drops
and never part from their inventory.

If we usually see in our games very high amounts of scrolls of identify we
can be sure they are *not* from monster equipment, and the same is true for
the scroll of enchant weapon. (They are from the same generation class.)

If you find very huge numbers of scrolls of create monster or teleportation,
those are (as opposed to identify and enchant weapon) *not* clearly separable
WRT having been created in monster equipment or from death-drops; but this is
completely irrelevant for the numbers of scrolls of the types which we were
discussing, i.e. from those that can *not* occur in monster equipment.

From the amount of found scrolls of teleportation you cannot derive any
number of expected to find number of scrolls of identify (or enchant weapon),
because the former stem from more generation sources than the latter (random
and monster equipment); the latter are only defined by the random generation
probabilities.

If you observe (in the long run) the numbers of generated scrolls of enchant
weapon and identify then you will observe (on average) a relation of about
8:18, roughly reflecting their random generation probabilities of 18% and 8%.
(But you cannot make such a statement involving, say, scrolls of itentify
and teleportation.)

